entation plan, get approval, then execute -- building the expanded training dataset, updating the training notebook, adding red team tools to the agent, updating system prompts, and pushing everything to GitHub. Since the user tends to approve quickly and wants this done thoroughly, I'll draft a detailed but focused plan first. I also want to be realistic about what a 3B model can actually learn -- it can pick up exploit snippets, CWE classification, and attack chain reasoning with enough examples, but it won't match something like GPT-4 on complex multi-step reasoning.\n\nThe right split is: the model handles offensive thinking, payload generation, and classification, while the agent supplies tools like nmap and sqlmap for actual execution -- reasoning and action working together.","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"c:\\Users\\k4ran\\OneDrive\\Desktop\\smartAGENT\\data\\custom_cot\\security_cot.jsonl","EndLine":5,"toolAction":"Reading training format","toolSummary":"Current training data format"}}]}
